{
  "name": "ListKnowsItsElement",
  "comment": "A list of path knows its element (rulings 1-2). A list carrying Type={list, kind: path}\nbirths its [0] as a path. Written in formal so the builder's Type choice (today's unstable\n2-list/3-path baseline for `as list of path`) is out of it — the red is the runtime's:\ntoday the kind of a typed list is a bare string (`kind.name` fails) and the element isn't\nborn a path.",
